{
  "set": "dalaran/platform_hall",
  "rev": 1,
  "about": "Dalaran's shell family: the same slots, sizes, ids and placement as lordaeron/timber_relief, so the solver, plan.json and the composer carry over, in Dalaran's construction (red columns on the ground storey on a stepped stone plinth, white plaster in dark timber above, lattice windows, brackets under the eave, a violet tile skirt between storeys) and one concave hipped roof per body with upturned corners. Cores and fit-out are Lordaeron's parts (lordaeron/part/timber_relief).",
  "grid": {
    "post": 1,
    "bay": 2,
    "storey": 5,
    "relief": 1,
    "pitch": 2,
    "body": "3n + 1 wide and deep (7, 10, 13); the template adds the relief: +2, or +1 per party wall"
  },
  "palettes": "none yet: the modules carry Dalaran's materials",
  "placement": {
    "shell": "Modules are authored for the FRONT face: local x left to right as seen from outside, y 0 = the storey's sill/floor layer, z 0 = the wall on the body line, z 1 = the relief outside it. Positions i along a face count from its outside-left corner. Turns (quarter turns clockwise, seen from above) and the module's min corner, for a module w wide at position i, body W x D with its north-west corner at body (0, 0): front q0 at (i, D-1); back q2 at (W-i-w, -1); east q3 at (W-1, D-i-w); west q1 at (-1, i). One-layer party modules sit on the wall line (west at x 0). Corners (2 x 2) at front:0 q0 (-1, D-1), front:W-1 q3 (W-1, D-1), back:0 q2 (W-1, -1), back:W-1 q1 (-1, -1); corner_party (1 x 2) at front:i q0 (i, D-1), back:i q2 (W-1-i, -1). Corners belong to the front and back faces; sides run i = 1..D-2.",
    "storeys": "storey s has its layer 0 at y = 2 + 5s (layers 0-1 are the foundation, every cell of body and relief); the roof starts at 2 + 5 * storeys",
    "plan": "Cores and fit-outs at body (x, z) of their min corner, y = the storey's layer 0 + dy. Cores replace the floor and room air under them (their holes win).",
    "roof": "hip: one module, roof_hip_<W>x<D>, over the body's relief outline and the eave (2) all round, its min corner at body (-1 - 2, -1 - 2) at y = 2 + 5 * storeys. The template is 2 wider on every side than a Lordaeron one: shift every other placement by +2 in x and z.",
    "stack": "none: Dalaran's roof is unbroken (the hearth stays; chimney bays are plaster piers)"
  },
  "sockets": {
    "note": "Faces meet when labels match or a pair allows it. Shell modules alternate post | bay along a face, corners at the ends.",
    "post": {
      "left": "bay",
      "right": "bay",
      "down": "floor_line|foundation",
      "up": "floor_line|eave"
    },
    "bay": {
      "left": "post|corner",
      "right": "post|corner",
      "down": "floor_line|foundation",
      "up": "floor_line|eave"
    },
    "corner": {
      "along_front": "bay",
      "along_side": "bay",
      "down": "floor_line|foundation",
      "up": "floor_line|eave"
    }
  },
  "pairs": [
    [
      "floor_line",
      "floor_line"
    ],
    [
      "eave",
      "roof"
    ]
  ],
  "limits": [
    {
      "module": "bay_door_ground",
      "per": "front",
      "exactly": 1
    },
    {
      "module": "chimney_*",
      "per": "house",
      "at_most": 1,
      "note": "on the west side's middle post (or the party wall); the hearth behind it"
    }
  ],
  "stacks": [
    [
      "chimney_ground",
      "chimney_upper",
      "chimney_stack"
    ],
    [
      "core_*_bottom",
      "core_*_mid",
      "core_*_top"
    ]
  ],
  "rooms": {
    "chamber": {
      "beds": "1 to 3 a floor (bed fit-out, heads north)"
    },
    "hall": {
      "hearth": 1
    },
    "work": {
      "workstation": "by trade (a marker: block any)"
    },
    "stair": {
      "core": "stair2x5 | stair3x3"
    },
    "store": {}
  },
  "behind": "bay_window(_box) over chamber or hall; bay_landing over the stair core and on ground-storey sides; bay_shop over shop/work/hall on the ground front; bay_plain over a store; chimney over the hearth",
  "weights": "per module JSON; bay_window 4, bay_window_box 2 (street fronts, raise by tier), bay_landing 3, bay_plain 1",
